## Why This Is Asked

Tests for multi-tenant access control require validating isolation, policy latency, and resilience under failure. This question probes practical thinking about RBAC/ABAC, caching, and auditability in production-like conditions.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and ABAC/RBAC enforcement
- Cache invalidation strategies and TTLs (Redis)
- Admin API driven policy propagation latency
- Failure handling: DB outages, cache misses, race conditions
- Audit logging and traceability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test: measure policy propagation latency after Admin API update
async function testPolicyPropagationLatency(api, adminApi, token) {
  const t0 = Date.now();
  await api.get(`/tenants/42/users/7`, { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } });
  const t1 = Date.now();
  const latency = t1 - t0;
  console.log('propagation latency (ms):', latency);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure cross-region propagation latency for policy changes?
- How would you validate that policy changes cannot be bypassed via token tampering or cache poisoning?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests reliability of composite APIs with dependent services.

## Key Concepts
- Downstream latency, timeouts, partial failures, circuit breakers
- Idempotent retries, exponential backoff, observability
- End-to-end timing and schema validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test using jest + nock
const nock = require('nock');
const request = require('supertest');
const app = require('../app');
test('partial data when one downstream times out', async () => {
  nock('http://sales').get('/daily').delay(3000).reply(200, {sales: 1000});
  nock('http://customers').get('/daily').reply(200, {customers: 50});
  const res = await request(app).get('/reports/daily');
  expect(res.statusCode).toBe(200);
  expect(res.body).toHaveProperty('sales');
  expect(res.headers).toHaveProperty('x-downstream-warn');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test circuit-breaker behavior under sustained latency?
- What metrics would you validate in your observability stack?

